        "text": "Digital twins are a real time virtual representation of physical objects or processes. The Metaverse will likely include all the above elements, each serving different purposes. But one thing is blockchain and cryptocurrencies are likely essential components of the Metaverse. When we work, socialize, and purchase digital items in the Metaverse, we need a secure way of showing ownership of digital items and transferring such ownership between people regardless of the platform they exist on. Digital money that can cross borders easily will be needed for a global, borderless metaverse. We will also want to participate in governance if the Metaverse is a large part of our lives. Future iterations of current blockchain technologies are what will be used in the Metaverse, although we can already see their applicability today. For example, blockchain based wallets will enable people to have digital identities and own digital assets.",
